      "content": "For a suburban tax protest, a typical headline might read: \"Suburban Residents Unite for Peaceful Overhaul of Tax Legislation,\" framing the event as orderly, constructive, and community-oriented. In contrast, coverage of inner-city unrest involving minority youth and police often appears as: \"Clashes Erupt Following Police Charges Against Young Protesters,\" implicitly highlighting disorder, conflict, and aggression. These examples vividly demonstrate how the same core action—people gathering to express dissent—can be linguistically constructed as either a rational civic duty or an explosion of chaos based solely on context and demographics.",
